msgstr "Open in a browser on your PC or mobile device (same home network):[CR][B]%s[/B][CR]and paste the copied text there."

msgctxt "#31489"
msgid "[B]%(source)s - taking over a browser session[/B][CR][CR]1. Open https://%(domain)s in a browser (PC recommended) and complete the check until the normal page appears.[CR]2. Press F12, open the [B]Network[/B] tab, reload the page (F5), right-click the first line and choose [B]Copy > Copy as cURL[/B] (Chrome/Edge: 'Copy as cURL (bash)').[CR]3. Choose 'Paste from PC or mobile device' here and paste the text on the page shown - or paste it directly in Kodi.[CR][CR]Baka reads the cookie (%(cookies)s) and the matching user agent automatically.[CR][CR][B]Good to know[/B][CR]- Cookie and user agent belong together; 'as cURL' contains both.[CR]- The cookie usually only works for the internet connection (IP) it was obtained with: browser and Kodi must use the same connection (no VPN on only one device).[CR]- Cookies expire after hours to days depending on the site; then repeat. Fully automatic renewal is only possible with FlareSolverr (Settings > General > Network)."
msgstr "[B]%(source)s - taking over a browser session[/B][CR][CR]1. Open https://%(domain)s in a browser (PC recommended) and complete the check until the normal page appears.[CR]2. Press F12, open the [B]Network[/B] tab, reload the page (F5), right-click the first line and choose [B]Copy > Copy as cURL[/B] (Chrome/Edge: 'Copy as cURL (bash)').[CR]3. Choose 'Paste from PC or mobile device' here and paste the text on the page shown - or paste it directly in Kodi.[CR][CR]Baka reads the cookie (%(cookies)s) and the matching user agent automatically.[CR][CR][B]Good to know[/B][CR]- Cookie and user agent belong together; 'as cURL' contains both.[CR]- The cookie usually only works for the internet connection (IP) it was obtained with: browser and Kodi must use the same connection (no VPN on only one device).[CR]- Cookies expire after hours to days depending on the site; then repeat. Fully automatic renewal is only possible with FlareSolverr (Settings > General > Network)."

